{
  "$schema_note": "Golem colossus physics/assembly manifest, v3 (2026-08-21, ticket #713). Units: METRES and CUBIC METRES. Y-up, creature faces +Z. Rest pose = out_v3/golem.fbx exactly as delivered. See README_engine.md. EVERY number here was re-measured from the v3 scene after rigging - none carried forward from v2.1 on faith. They agree with v2.1 to 3 decimals, which is the proof that adding the animation rig did not disturb the geometry.",
  "whats_new_in_v3": "The asset now carries an animation skeleton (17 joints, prefix jnt_). Chunk MESHES and their golem_<segment> transforms are unchanged and undeformed - there is NO skinning anywhere. Each golem_<segment> group is now a child of its jnt_<segment> joint, so the joint IS the articulation node and the joint's world position IS the joint pivot. Physics consumers can ignore the joints entirely and use the chunk list below; animation consumers drive the joints.",
  "density_note": "mass values numerically equal solid volume in m^3 (density 1.0). The engine owns the real density constant. Suggested: kiln-fired earth ~1900-2200 kg/m^3.",
  "conventions": {
    "up": "+Y",
    "forward": "+Z",
    "hinge_axis_all_joints": [1.0, 0.0, 0.0],
    "rotation_sign": "positive X rotation moves a segment's LOWER end backward (-Z). Knee flexion is +, hip flexion (leg forward) is -, torso forward pitch is +. VERIFIED on the v3 rig: jnt_torso rx +10 moved jnt_head from (0,3.18,0.10) to (0,3.145,0.295), i.e. the upper body pitches forward.",
    "limits_are_relative_to_rest": "0 deg = the delivered rest pose. Ranges are [lo, hi] about the hinge axis, in the chunk's parent frame.",
    "joint_frames": "every jnt_* has jointOrient = (0,0,0) and a world-axis-aligned frame (measured: max world-axes error 0.0). So a joint's local rx IS the sagittal hinge - the same convention as the chunk data. This is deliberate; see NOTES.md."
  },
